meta {
  name: Rename the topic
  type: http
  seq: 25
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/curriculum-nodes/{{curriculumTopicId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Prime factorisation and LCM",
    "sequence": 2
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.title: eq Prime factorisation and LCM
  res.body.sequence: eq 2
}

docs {
  Nodes are patched on their own route, not under the curriculum, because that
  is where they are reached from: a client editing an outline has node ids, not
  a syllabus id and an index into it.

  curriculum_id is refused here with 422. Re-parenting a node into another
  syllabus by patching one field would move its placements with it, silently,
  and the content mapped to this topic would start answering questions asked of
  a different class.

  Renaming is safe. The placements in folder 11 point at the node id, so a
  topic can be worded better without anything mapped to it moving.
}
